Linux kernel
============

There are several guides for kernel developers and users. These guides can
be rendered in a number of formats, like HTML and PDF. Please read
Documentation/admin-guide/README.rst first.

In order to build the documentation, use ``make htmldocs`` or
``make pdfdocs``.  The formatted documentation can also be read online at:

    https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/

There are various text files in the Documentation/ subdirectory,
several of them using the Restructured Text markup notation.
See Documentation/00-INDEX for a list of what is contained in each file.

Please read the Documentation/process/changes.rst file, as it contains the
requirements for building and running the kernel, and information about
the problems which may result by upgrading your kernel.

DroidSpaces compatibility (Redmi Note 5 Pro / whyred)
=====================================================

This fork tracks the SDM660 San-Kernel 4.19 source on the ``back`` base
branch and documents a DroidSpaces-oriented configuration target for the
Xiaomi Redmi Note 5 Pro (codename ``whyred``).

The existing ``arch/arm64/configs/vendor/whyred-perf_defconfig`` already
enables several kernel facilities used by Android container and namespace
workloads, including:

* ``CONFIG_NAMESPACES`` with UTS, PID and user namespaces
* ``CONFIG_CGROUPS`` and CPU accounting/scheduling support
* ``CONFIG_SECCOMP``
* ``CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL`` and BPF JIT support
* ``CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS``

These options provide a useful baseline for DroidSpaces, which targets older
Android kernels and requires compatibility with legacy kernel interfaces.
They do not, by themselves, certify that every DroidSpaces feature works on
this device or ROM. In particular, the final kernel configuration, Android
vendor/userspace integration, SELinux policy, runtime behavior and boot
stability must be checked on the target Android 16 ROM. This repository has
not been represented as device-tested or as a verified working DroidSpaces
build merely by adding this documentation.

Build starting point:

.. code-block:: console

    make O=out ARCH=arm64 vendor/whyred-perf_defconfig

Review the resulting ``out/.config`` against the DroidSpaces requirements
before building or flashing. Keep the device-specific ``whyred`` defconfig as
the base; do not substitute another SDM660 device's defconfig.

Credits and upstream
====================

* **San-Kernel / SDM660 kernel source:** Santhosh (``user-why-red``) and the
  contributors to the original ``android_kernel_xiaomi_sdm660_419`` source
  (https://github.com/user-why-red/android_kernel_xiaomi_sdm660_419).
* **Linux kernel:** Linus Torvalds and the worldwide Linux kernel
  contributors. See ``CREDITS`` and the in-tree licensing files for the
  broader contributor and copyright record.
* **Xiaomi SDM660 community:** device and platform contributors whose work
  supports the SDM660 family, including ``whyred``.
* **DroidSpaces:** the DroidSpaces project and its developers, including
  DroidSpaces project (https://github.com/ravindu644/Droidspaces-OSS).
  DroidSpaces is a separate project; this kernel fork is not an official DroidSpaces release.

This fork retains the original kernel licensing and attribution. Consult
``COPYING``, ``LICENSES/`` and individual source-file headers before
redistributing modified binaries or source.
